# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads for the API container.
#
# This file matters more than it looks: without it gcloud falls back to
# the top-level .gitignore only - it does NOT read nested ones like
# web/.gitignore - so web/.next/ and web/node_modules/ were being
# uploaded, and the deploy died on the dev server's lock file
# (PermissionError: web\.next\dev\lock).
#
# Everything the API actually needs is listed in the Dockerfile's COPY
# lines; this just keeps the upload to roughly that.

.git/
.gitignore

# The frontend is its own Cloud Run service, deployed from web/.
web/

# Local state and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.mechnari_runtime/
.claude/

# Python build/cache artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Not needed in the runtime image
test_*.py
docs/
*.md
!requirements.txt

# Working documents that live alongside the code but are not part of it.
#
# Excluded for correctness, and also because a file open in Word or
# Acrobat is LOCKED on Windows: gcloud reads every file it uploads, and
# one it cannot read kills the whole deploy with
# `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied`. That is what happened
# with "Patchamomma 2026 Touchpoint 3 FINAL Form.docx" - the deploy
# failed because a document was open in another window, which is a
# miserable thing to debug from the error alone.
*.docx
*.pdf
*.pptx
*.xlsx
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
